.\" groff -man -Tascii kobject_uevent.9
.TH KOBJECT_UEVENT 9 "March 2026" "Substrate Kernel" "Kernel Developer's Manual"
.SH NAME
kobject_uevent, kobject_uevent_dump \- queue and inspect kernel device-model events
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/kobject.h>
.PP
.BI "void kobject_uevent(const char *" action ", const char *" subsystem ", const char *" name ");"
.BI "size_t kobject_uevent_dump(char *" buf ", size_t " size ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B kobject_uevent
interface records lightweight device-model lifecycle events inside a bounded
kernel ring buffer.
Each event is recorded as a single textual line containing the action,
subsystem, and device name.
.PP
The current implementation is intended for low-cost kernel diagnostics and for
export through
.BR /proc/device-events .
It is not a netlink-compatible transport.
.PP
.B kobject_uevent_dump
serializes the retained event ring into the caller-supplied buffer in FIFO
order.
When the ring is full, the oldest events are discarded.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.B kobject_uevent
returns no value.
.B kobject_uevent_dump
returns the number of bytes that would be written.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR proc (5),
.BR device_register (9),
.BR driver_attach (9)
